# NOTE: Upstream ignores every wrap-fetched subproject here (with a `/*/*`
# pattern plus one line per directory), because it re-fetches them from their
# wraps at build time. This port tracks them instead, for two reasons:
#
#   1. Two of them are patched. `vst3` is SDK 3.8.0 with the Haiku platform port
#      and the Winelib fixes already applied (its wrap, which pointed at a stock
#      3.7.7, has been deleted). `ghc_filesystem` has a one-hunk fix so it picks
#      POSIX mode instead of Windows mode under winegcc. Neither survives a
#      re-fetch, so neither can be left untracked.
#   2. Builds happen on the Haiku laptop, which should not have to reach the
#      network to clone six git repositories mid-build. Tracking them keeps a
#      fresh checkout buildable offline.
#
# Consequently `meson subprojects update` must not be run against these -- it
# would discard the patches. Re-vendor deliberately instead.
#
# The upstream pattern is inverted here rather than negated, because `/*/*`
# excludes the subdirectories themselves and git cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded.

# Meson's download cache, and asio, which comes from `pkgman install asio`
# rather than from its wrap on this platform.
/packagecache/
/asio/
